# STIG RHEL-09-654020: RHEL 9 must audit all uses of the chown, fchown, fchownat, and lchown system cal
# STIG ID: V-258178 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `r9-rhel-09-654020-audit-perm-mod-chown-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `rocky9`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG RHEL-09-654020: RHEL 9 must audit all uses of the chown, fchown, fchownat, and lchown system cal`
    description `RHEL 9 must audit all uses of the chown, fchown, fchownat, and lchown system calls.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `rhel9,stig,disa-stig`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:RHEL-09-654020,NIST-800-53:AU-12,NIST-800-53:AU-3,NIST-800-53:AU-3(1),NIST-800-53:MA-4(1)(A)`
    control_objective `AU-12`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Rocky9:localhost:os-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA STIG guidance for RHEL-09-654020.`

    component_id `comp-r9-os`

    impl_AU_12 `This control is validated by checking the content of /etc/audit/rules.d/audit.rules for the required configuration setting.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target_file
        path `/etc/audit/rules.d/audit.rules`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE content_check
        content string contains `-S lchown,fchown,chown,fchownat`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN file_content
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF content_check
            OBJECT_REF target_file
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
